WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.738
Welcome back to your Danish citizenship exam companion.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:10.224
This is Chapter Three, Episode Four: Danish business life and trade with the rest of the world.

3
00:00:10.774 --> 00:00:13.811
How does a country get from ploughs to pharmaceuticals?

4
00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:27.811
Like most other wealthy countries, Denmark has gradually developed from being an agricultural society to an industrial society, and then, in the last 50 years, to being a so-called knowledge and service society.

5
00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:47.610
That is, we have gone from an economy that is primarily based on the production of goods, to being to a higher degree dependent on highly educated labour, with a focus on using knowledge and getting new ideas, and on the production of services, for example the banking sector, IT support, research or education.

6
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.797
Until the end of the 1800s, the majority of the population worked in agriculture.

7
00:00:53.748 --> 00:01:02.585
But from the 1870s, industry and crafts grew quickly, the population moved from countryside to town, and the towns grew.

8
00:01:02.585 --> 00:01:10.060
Agriculture remained important, however, especially because agricultural goods made up most of Denmark's exports.

9
00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:20.873
The focus was on high-quality animal production, for example meat, butter and cheese, within the framework of the many cooperative associations' dairies and slaughterhouses.

10
00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:27.876
Right up until the end of the 1950s, agricultural goods made up more than half of Denmark's exports.

11
00:01:28.426 --> 00:01:39.726
Agricultural production is still large, but since the 1950s there has been a dramatic increase in efficiency, and today only about two percent of the workforce work in agriculture itself.

12
00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:43.101
But agriculture is still an important export industry.

13
00:01:43.101 --> 00:01:56.982
People often speak in that connection of a food cluster, fødevareklynge, because fewer are employed in agriculture itself and more are employed in processing, transport, sales, marketing and product development.

14
00:01:57.532 --> 00:02:00.469
Agriculture is also changing in other ways.

15
00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:11.532
Agriculture has been criticised for being too efficient in an unfortunate way, among other things because too much poison is used on the fields to kill weeds, fungi and insects.

16
00:02:11.532 --> 00:02:24.019
That has contributed to a beginning green transition, so that Denmark today is the country with the largest share of agriculture, 11.1 percent in 2024, run as organic farming.

17
00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:36.408
Organic farming is run, among other things, without the use of chemical pesticides and artificial fertiliser, and the animals have more room in the stables and better opportunity to get out into the open air.

18
00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:45.145
The first big wave of industrialisation in Denmark took place at the end of the 1800s and the beginning of the 1900s.

19
00:02:45.096 --> 00:02:56.270
Progress continued, but at a somewhat slower pace, until the second big wave of industrialisation, which was from the end of the 1950s to around 1970.

20
00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:04.221
From the beginning of the 1970s, the share of people employed in industry fell, just as had earlier happened in agriculture.

21
00:03:04.221 --> 00:03:06.921
Instead, the service sector grew.

22
00:03:06.921 --> 00:03:16.758
Today, almost four out of five people employed work in private or public service companies, for example in tourism, health, consulting or education.

23
00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:20.946
About 30 percent of employees in Denmark work in the public sector.

24
00:03:20.946 --> 00:03:28.290
That is roughly one third, so most employees, about two thirds, work in the private sector, not the public sector.

25
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:36.252
The production of agricultural and industrial goods has, however, risen, even though the number of employees has fallen.

26
00:03:36.203 --> 00:03:42.203
That is especially due to the mechanisation of production and the rapid technological development in these sectors.

27
00:03:42.203 --> 00:03:47.953
Denmark has previously been characterised by most companies being small or medium-sized.

28
00:03:47.953 --> 00:03:56.703
That is still true, but more companies have come along that take up a lot of space on the world market in the industries where Denmark is especially strong.

29
00:03:56.703 --> 00:04:12.815
This applies for example to food, where dairies and slaughterhouses are gathered into international giants: Danish Crown was in 2025 the world's second largest pig slaughterhouse, and Arla was in 2025 among the ten largest dairies.

30
00:04:12.815 --> 00:04:17.580
Carlsberg was in 2025 the world's fourth largest brewery.

31
00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:21.168
Denmark has a large pharmaceutical industry.

32
00:04:21.118 --> 00:04:28.318
Several Danish pharmaceutical companies have a large share of the world market, of which Novo Nordisk is the largest.

33
00:04:28.318 --> 00:04:35.718
The location of Novo Nordisk in Denmark is of very great importance for the Danish economy, exports and employment.

34
00:04:36.268 --> 00:04:40.193
Denmark also makes over one third of the world's hearing aids.

35
00:04:40.143 --> 00:04:52.536
The three biggest Danish producers, GN Store Nord, with GN Resound, William Demant, with Oticon, and Widex, are among the biggest hearing aid producers in the world.

36
00:04:53.086 --> 00:04:57.136
In addition, LEGO is one of the world's biggest toy groups.

37
00:04:57.086 --> 00:05:03.599
LEGO was founded in 1932, and is an abbreviation of "leg godt", which means "play well".

38
00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:06.311
The headquarters is in Billund in Jutland.

39
00:05:06.311 --> 00:05:09.042
LEGO is known for making plastic bricks.

40
00:05:09.592 --> 00:05:22.716
Denmark has always been a big seafaring nation and had, in 2024, the world's tenth largest merchant fleet, and the world's second largest container shipping company in 2025, Mærsk.

41
00:05:23.266 --> 00:05:25.891
Add to that companies from the green sector.

42
00:05:25.841 --> 00:05:31.141
The Danish Vestas was in 2024 the world's largest wind turbine producer.

43
00:05:31.141 --> 00:05:39.558
Denmark is also very strong when it comes to energy savings, which can for example be insulation or extra energy-efficient products.

44
00:05:40.108 --> 00:05:42.620
Now to trade with the outside world.

45
00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:48.370
Denmark has a very open economy, where trade with other countries plays a very big role.

46
00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.095
Exports make up about half of the country's total production.

47
00:05:52.095 --> 00:06:02.058
That is naturally also because Denmark is a small country, and trade with other countries, not least the neighbouring countries, therefore takes up a lot of space.

48
00:06:02.058 --> 00:06:11.045
Germany is the country Denmark imports, buys, most from, and the USA is the country Denmark exports, sells, most to.

49
00:06:11.045 --> 00:06:16.344
Overall, however, exports to other EU countries are clearly greater than to the USA.

50
00:06:16.894 --> 00:06:27.706
In 2025, Denmark's seven biggest trading partners were the following, in their share of the value of Denmark's total foreign trade, imports and exports.

51
00:06:27.656 --> 00:06:30.531
The USA, 14.1 percent.

52
00:06:30.531 --> 00:06:33.356
Germany, 12.7 percent.

53
00:06:33.356 --> 00:06:36.294
Sweden, 7.8 percent.

54
00:06:36.294 --> 00:06:39.069
The Netherlands, 5.4 percent.

55
00:06:39.069 --> 00:06:41.994
The United Kingdom, 5.2 percent.

56
00:06:41.994 --> 00:06:44.431
China, 4.8 percent.

57
00:06:44.431 --> 00:06:46.519
And Norway, 4.0 percent.

58
00:06:46.519 --> 00:06:54.994
So measured by total trade, imports plus exports, the USA is now Denmark's biggest trading partner, ahead of Germany.

59
00:06:54.994 --> 00:07:00.231
Germany is still the country Denmark buys most from, the biggest source of imports.

60
00:07:00.231 --> 00:07:05.370
Older exam questions that give Germany as the biggest trading partner are out of date.

61
00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:12.682
Danish governments have in modern times almost always been in favour of as much free trade between countries as possible.

62
00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:17.595
Since the 1990s Denmark has also done better in international competition.

63
00:07:17.595 --> 00:07:23.520
In the same period, Danish exports have in practically all years been higher than imports.

64
00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:30.832
Denmark is a member of a number of international organisations that, like the EU, also work for more free trade.

65
00:07:30.832 --> 00:07:41.004
This applies for example to the OECD, the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development, and the WTO, the World Trade Organization.

66
00:07:41.554 --> 00:07:46.541
Economic globalisation has brought about big changes on the Danish labour market.

67
00:07:46.491 --> 00:07:51.654
Many companies have moved parts of their production to places in the world where wages are lower.

68
00:07:51.654 --> 00:07:57.941
Not only to China, but also to, for example, Eastern Europe or other European countries.

69
00:07:57.941 --> 00:08:07.554
Up to now, companies have, however, typically kept some important functions in Denmark, for example the development of new products, sales and management.

70
00:08:07.554 --> 00:08:12.246
In return, new big markets have also emerged for Danish products.

71
00:08:12.796 --> 00:08:15.083
Here is your recap for Episode Four.

72
00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:23.721
Denmark went from agricultural society to industrial society, and in the last 50 years to a knowledge and service society.

73
00:08:23.721 --> 00:08:31.183
Until the end of the 1800s most people worked in agriculture; from the 1870s industry and crafts grew.

74
00:08:31.183 --> 00:08:36.321
Agricultural goods were more than half of exports until the end of the 1950s.

75
00:08:36.321 --> 00:08:40.308
Today only about two percent of the workforce works in agriculture.

76
00:08:40.308 --> 00:08:46.883
Denmark has the largest share of organic agriculture, 11.1 percent in 2024.

77
00:08:46.883 --> 00:08:55.058
Industrialisation came in two waves: the end of the 1800s, and the end of the 1950s to about 1970.

78
00:08:55.058 --> 00:09:01.421
Almost four out of five employees work in services, and about 30 percent of employees in the public sector.

79
00:09:01.421 --> 00:09:28.633
Danish Crown is the world's second largest pig slaughterhouse, Arla among the ten largest dairies, Carlsberg the fourth largest brewery, Novo Nordisk the largest Danish pharmaceutical company, Denmark makes over one third of the world's hearing aids, LEGO was founded in 1932 and is based in Billund, Mærsk is the second largest container shipping company, and Vestas the largest wind turbine producer.

80
00:09:28.633 --> 00:09:30.921
Exports are about half of production.

81
00:09:30.921 --> 00:09:36.208
Germany is the biggest source of imports, the USA the biggest export market.

82
00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:56.383
The top trading partners in 2025, with the USA the biggest in total trade: the USA 14.1 percent, Germany 12.7, Sweden 7.8, the Netherlands 5.4, the United Kingdom 5.2, China 4.8 and Norway 4.0.

83
00:09:56.383 --> 00:10:00.288
Denmark is a member of the OECD and the WTO.

84
00:10:00.838 --> 00:10:03.438
Now it is time for your exam practice.

85
00:10:03.388 --> 00:10:08.300
These are real questions from past Danish citizenship exams on what you just heard.

86
00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:15.786
For each one, I will read the question and the choices, then pause so you can pick your answer, and then I will give you the correct answer.

87
00:10:16.336 --> 00:10:17.586
Question 1.

88
00:10:17.536 --> 00:10:20.999
How large a share of those in employment work in the public sector?

89
00:10:20.999 --> 00:10:23.411
Option A: About one third.

90
00:10:23.411 --> 00:10:25.812
Option B: About two thirds.
[DA] Hvor stor en del af de beskæftigede arbejder i den offentlige sektor?  A: Ca. en tredjedel  |  B: Ca. to tredjedele

91
00:10:32.362 --> 00:10:35.050
The answer is A: About one third.

92
00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:39.270
It appeared in the June 2020 and November 2021 exams.
[DA] ✔ A: Ca. en tredjedel

93
00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.070
Question 2.

94
00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.908
Is the majority of employees in Denmark employed in the public sector?

95
00:10:44.908 --> 00:10:46.533
Option A: Yes.

96
00:10:46.533 --> 00:10:48.192
Option B: No.
[DA] Er flertallet af lønmodtagerne i Danmark ansat i den offentlige sektor?  A: Ja  |  B: Nej

97
00:10:54.742 --> 00:10:56.742
The answer is B: No.

98
00:10:56.692 --> 00:10:59.370
It appeared in the May 2025 exam.
[DA] ✔ B: Nej

99
00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.258
Question 3.

100
00:11:01.208 --> 00:11:05.158
Which of the following companies is known for producing wind turbines?

101
00:11:05.158 --> 00:11:07.620
Option A: Novo Nordisk.

102
00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.508
Option B: Mærsk.

103
00:11:09.508 --> 00:11:11.676
Option C: Vestas.
[DA] Hvilken af følgende virksomheder er kendt for at producere vindmøller?  A: Novo Nordisk  |  B: Mærsk  |  C: Vestas

104
00:11:18.226 --> 00:11:20.526
The answer is C: Vestas.

105
00:11:20.476 --> 00:11:23.454
It appeared in the November 2025 exam.
[DA] ✔ C: Vestas

106
00:11:24.004 --> 00:11:25.304
Question 4.

107
00:11:25.254 --> 00:11:28.129
Where did most people work around 1850?

108
00:11:28.129 --> 00:11:30.067
Option A: In industry.

109
00:11:30.067 --> 00:11:32.179
Option B: In agriculture.

110
00:11:32.179 --> 00:11:34.104
Option C: In fishing.
[DA] Hvor arbejdede der flest mennesker omkring 1850?  A: I industrien  |  B: I landbruget  |  C: I fiskeriet

111
00:11:40.654 --> 00:11:43.079
The answer is B: In agriculture.

112
00:11:43.029 --> 00:11:47.202
It appeared in the May 2024 and June 2026 exams.
[DA] ✔ B: I landbruget

113
00:11:47.752 --> 00:11:49.215
Question 5.

114
00:11:49.165 --> 00:11:58.265
Which country does Denmark have the largest trade with, imports and exports combined, according to the 2026 edition of the learning material?

115
00:11:58.265 --> 00:12:02.665
This is an updated question, because older exam keys said Germany.

116
00:12:02.665 --> 00:12:04.440
Option A: China.

117
00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.665
Option B: The USA.

118
00:12:06.665 --> 00:12:08.748
Option C: Germany.
[DA] Hvilket af følgende lande har Danmark størst samhandel (import og eksport) med? [opdateret til lærematerialet 2026]  A: Kina  |  B: USA  |  C: Tyskland

119
00:12:15.298 --> 00:12:17.673
The answer is B: The USA.

120
00:12:17.623 --> 00:12:30.702
This is not an old exam answer: older exam keys said Germany, but in the 2026 material the USA, with 14.1 percent, is ahead of Germany, with 12.7 percent.
[DA] ✔ B: USA

121
00:12:31.252 --> 00:12:33.015
That's the end of this part.

122
00:12:32.965 --> 00:12:34.032
Well done.

